A||N||10||turbo86se||rear suspension swap?||||5||
Z||000000||turbo86se||01-08-2000||03:29 PM||||<BR>Hey everyone, in a month or two I plan to convert my 88 coupe to a V6. I've already got an engine, low mileage Formula V6, and I'm going to start purchasing suspension parts now. My concern is the rear springs. I've heard the stock 4 cyl springs are soft, and may not be the best choice to run with the V6. I do have a 85SE V6 parts car. Would I be able to use those rear springs on my 88? Are there any differences between the 85-88 rear shocks? Many thanks!!  -joel||||reg||5
Z||000001||mrfiero||01-08-2000||05:05 PM||||The springs from any '84-'87 Fiero will not work on your '88 coupe (and vice versa).  They are completely different sizes/shapes and are not interchangable.  You will need to find some springs from an '88 Formula or GT or buy a set of lowered springs (the Fiero Store sells them). <P>The rear struts themselves are the same for all years of Fieros.  Some parts places say that the '88s are different, but they're not.  I bought a set of KYB shocks & struts and the struts are listed as being for '84-'87 Fieros, but they work just fine on my Formula.<P>I do have a set of '88 V-6 rear springs (from a Formula)....LMK if you need them.     ||||reg||1
Z||000002||turbo86se||01-08-2000||05:12 PM||||mrfiero, how much are you asking for the springs?  Did you lower your Formula? If so, how does the ride compare to stock? TIA, joel||||reg||1
Z||000003||mrfiero||01-08-2000||05:23 PM||||I don't know.....how does $40 sound?  I should have a loose set lying around, but I'm not sure.  I do have a set still on a Formula (hit on drivers side), so I know I have at least one set.<P>I used the lowered springs from the Fiero Store on my Formula.  I also have poly bushings, KYB shocks/struts and bigger poly endlink bushings, etc.  It handles very nice, but it does ride a little rougher than a stock Fiero.  I personally don't mind the harshness, but you might....I don't know.<P>I am saving up for the Ryane coilover suspension and big brakes....that is the ultimate in Fiero handling!  I owned an '85 GT with this set-up and it would out corner/out brake just about everything out there.<P>LMK on the springs.||||reg||10
Z||000004||turbo86se||01-08-2000||05:55 PM||||40 for the springs sounds great!  On the Formula that's hit in the front, would you have any other parts available? Like front springs, gauge cluster? Thanks!  GO SKINS!!!||||reg||1
Z||000005||SCCA FIERO||01-08-2000||06:00 PM||||mrfiero, that Formula still have the rear swaybar? If so and you are willing to sell I would like a crack at buying it.||||reg||1
Z||000006||mrfiero||01-08-2000||07:57 PM||||turbo86se,<P>Yes, it still has the front springs.  Right now it is still a complete car (minus the wheels).<P>I won't bore you with details, but the tranny (5-sp.) self-destructed and was parked in front of a friends house for a few months.  The day before (no kidding) I was to tow it away to start fixing it a drunk driver smashed into the side of it.  I figure he had to of been going 40 MPH.  It destroyed the door and really mangled the B pillar/door jam area.  <P>If you want all 4 springs then figure on $75 + whatever the shipping is.  LMK if that sounds OK to you.  <P><BR>SCCA FIERO,<P>It still has the rear sway bar, but I am holding it for someone else right now.  If that falls through you'll be the first to know.||||reg||6
Z||000007||SCCA FIERO||01-08-2000||08:56 PM||||Hey cool. If the deal falls through I will be here to catch it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">. Also, I am trying to locate the cable brackets for the Getrag. I can get a complet set of brackets (not cables just the brackets) made of steel from Rodney Dickman for about $80. I am willing to pay $40 for a set of used ones. Or what ever you think may be a deal... lemme know.||||reg||6
Z||000008||turbo86se||01-09-2000||02:22 AM||||mrfiero, 75 for front and back springs also sounds great. Let me check my finances and I'll get back to you very soon. Have you sold the air cleaner assembly? If not, how much for everything I'd need to install it on my Fiero? <BR>Thanks again,   -joel||||reg||1
Z||000009||mrfiero||01-09-2000||03:26 PM||||turbo86se,<P>No hurry....LMK when you're ready.<P>I have *several* V-6 air cleaner assemblies, so no problem there either.  I'm assuming you  will need "the works", so figure another $25.  This would be for the air cleaner housing & it's base, air inlet tube, the water separater and assorted misc. stuff associated with the air intake.<P>||||reg||14
